# 🏗️ InfraSight / Pulse — Production Backend Architecture Plan

> **Stack:** Node.js 22 · TypeScript 5 · Express/Fastify · PostgreSQL 16 · Redis 7 · Prisma ORM · OpenAI · WebSocket (ws) · BullMQ · Docker · Zod

---

## Overview

This document defines the **complete production-grade backend** that mirrors every feature of the Pulse frontend. The backend is a standalone monorepo package (`/backend`) placed **beside** the existing frontend. No existing frontend files are touched.

```
infrasight/
├── src/                  ← existing frontend (untouched)
├── backend/              ← NEW: entire backend lives here
├── package.json          ← frontend
└── ...
```

---

## Tech Stack Decisions

| Layer | Choice | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Runtime | Node.js 22 LTS | ES modules, native fetch, top performance |
| Language | TypeScript 5 strict | Full type-safety end-to-end |
| Framework | **Fastify 5** | 3× faster than Express, built-in schema validation |
| ORM | **Prisma 5** | Type-safe queries, migrations, excellent Postgres support |
| Database | **PostgreSQL 16** | JSONB for payloads, TimescaleDB extension for time-series |
| Cache/Pub-Sub | **Redis 7** | Sessions, rate limiting, WebSocket pub-sub, BullMQ |
| Queue Engine | **BullMQ** | Production-grade job queues backed by Redis |
| AI | **OpenAI SDK + LangChain** | GPT-4o for anomaly detection, RCA, log analysis |
| Auth | **JWT (RS256) + Refresh tokens** | Stateless, scalable, stored in httpOnly cookies |
| Realtime | **WebSocket (ws) + Redis pub-sub** | Live metrics, event streams, alerts |
| Validation | **Zod** | Runtime schema validation for all DTOs |
| Email | **Resend** | Transactional emails (password reset, invites) |
| Logging | **Pino** | Structured JSON logging |
| Testing | **Vitest + Supertest** | Unit + integration tests |
| Containerization | **Docker + docker-compose** | Local dev + production parity |

