## Per-Module Internal Structure (Applied to ALL 18 modules)

Every single module follows the **exact same internal layout**:

```
modules/<module-name>/
├── <module>.controller.ts    ← HTTP handlers (thin, delegates to service)
├── <module>.service.ts       ← Business logic, orchestration
├── <module>.repository.ts    ← All DB queries (Prisma calls only here)
├── <module>.routes.ts        ← Route registration + middleware chain
├── <module>.schema.ts        ← Zod schemas (validation for all DTOs)
├── <module>.dto.ts           ← TypeScript types inferred from Zod schemas
├── <module>.model.ts         ← Prisma model type re-exports + domain types
└── index.ts                  ← barrel export
```

### Data Flow per Request

```
HTTP Request
    ↓
Route (Fastify route definition + auth middleware)
    ↓
Controller (parse & validate DTO via Zod)
    ↓
Service (business logic, calls other services if needed)
    ↓
Repository (Prisma query → PostgreSQL)
    ↓
Response DTO (serialized & returned)
```

